# NER-based PII Detection (Presidio + spaCy)
# spaCy model backing Presidio NER (tier 3 of the content filter).
#
# Declared here deliberately. It was previously installed on developer machines
# by hand and declared NOWHERE -- not in a requirements file, a Dockerfile, or a
# doc -- so the NER PII tier never ran in a built image, silently. Worse,
# NlpEngineProvider.create_engine() FETCHES a missing model at runtime rather
# than failing fast, which stalled CI until the job was cancelled.
#
# spaCy models are not published to PyPI, so this is a direct wheel URL. It is
# hash-verified like every other pin.
#
# ~382MB wheel / ~425MB installed. Set NER_SPACY_MODEL=en_core_web_md (32MB) for
# a smaller image at some cost in entity-detection accuracy; the code reads that
# env var and this pin only decides which model is present.
en_core_web_lg @ https://github.com/explosion/spacy-models/releases/download/en_core_web_lg-3.8.0/en_core_web_lg-3.8.0-py3-none-any.whl

presidio-analyzer>=2.2.364
